# data never enters git — raw meetings, transcripts, sandbox writes
# (data/* rather than data/ — git will not re-include a file whose parent directory
# is excluded, so the negation below only works if the directory itself is not)
data/*
# ...except the corpus manifest, which is metadata rather than content: without it a
# fresh clone has no record of what the audio is supposed to be (M2X-015)
!data/corpus.json
# real keys live in ~/.config, only .env.example is tracked
.env
# held-out labels are Evaluator-only until the gate (blind-labelling rule). The sealed
# set is committed as *ciphertext* so a reviewer can confirm the ten cases exist and were
# not edited between the freeze and the gate — an ignored directory proves neither.
# Plaintext beside it must never enter git. Same `dir/*` trick as data/ above: git will
# not re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
eval/labels/heldout/*
!eval/labels/heldout/*.age
!eval/labels/heldout/*.gpg
!eval/labels/heldout/.gitkeep
!eval/labels/heldout/README.md
# the integrity half of the seal (M2X-041). Ciphertext proves the set is recoverable;
# only this manifest proves it is unedited, because gpg salts every run and a *.gpg diff
# therefore cannot tell a re-seal from a content change. Digests leak nothing.
!eval/labels/heldout/seal-manifest.json
# the pre-M2X-030 path, kept ignored so an older checkout cannot leak a case through it
eval/heldout/
# the Phase 2 gate's answer key (M2X-045), sealed on the same terms as the held-out
# labels. Questions are public -- the system has to be asked them -- but a builder who can
# read the expected segments can tune retrieval until they come back, and a retrieval
# metric tuned against its own answer key measures nothing.
eval/rag/expected/*
!eval/rag/expected/*.gpg
!eval/rag/expected/seal-manifest.json
!eval/rag/expected/.gitkeep
!eval/rag/expected/README.md
# labels in progress, before the dev/held-out split has been drawn. Every case is
# plaintext here and ten of them are about to become the sealed set -- committing this
# directory would put the held-out cases in git history, and no later encryption can
# take them back out. Ignored so the seal cannot be lost before it is applied.
eval/labels/staging/
__pycache__/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
# local-only hotwords: client/project and personal names the public file must not carry
eval/vocab.local.txt

# local-only references: a verbatim reference transcript cannot be redacted without
# destroying the WER it exists to measure, so a meeting whose content is client work
# keeps its reference here instead of in the tracked snippet. Same rule as vocab.local.
eval/snippets/*.local.txt
